### Book Lending Service — sample requests
### Works with the IntelliJ HTTP Client and the VS Code "REST Client" extension.
### Start the stack first: docker compose up --build
### IDs below match the seed data (V2__seed_data.sql) on a fresh database.

@host = http://localhost:8080
@admin = admin admin123
@librarian = librarian librarian123
@alice = alice@example.com alice123
@bob = bob@example.com bob123

### Health (public)
GET {{host}}/actuator/health

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- Books

### List books, search by title (any authenticated user)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/books?title=design&page=0&size=5&sort=title,asc
Authorization: Basic {{alice}}

### Get one book
GET {{host}}/api/v1/books/1
Authorization: Basic {{alice}}

### Add a book (LIBRARIAN / ADMIN)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/books
Authorization: Basic {{librarian}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Clean Architecture",
  "author": "Robert C. Martin",
  "isbn": "978-0134494166",
  "totalCopies": 2
}

### Update a book (cannot drop totalCopies below copies on loan -> 409 COPIES_ON_LOAN)
PUT {{host}}/api/v1/books/1
Authorization: Basic {{librarian}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Clean Code",
  "author": "Robert C. Martin",
  "isbn": "9780132350884",
  "totalCopies": 4
}

### Validation error -> 400 with field errors
POST {{host}}/api/v1/books
Authorization: Basic {{librarian}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "",
  "author": "Nobody",
  "isbn": "123",
  "totalCopies": -1
}

### Member tries to add a book -> 403
POST {{host}}/api/v1/books
Authorization: Basic {{alice}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Not allowed",
  "author": "Alice",
  "isbn": "9780134494166",
  "totalCopies": 1
}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- Members

### List members (LIBRARIAN / ADMIN)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/members
Authorization: Basic {{librarian}}

### Alice reads her own profile (member 1)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/members/1
Authorization: Basic {{alice}}

### Alice reads Bob's profile -> 403
GET {{host}}/api/v1/members/2
Authorization: Basic {{alice}}

### Register a member
POST {{host}}/api/v1/members
Authorization: Basic {{librarian}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Dave Miller",
  "email": "dave@example.com"
}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- Loans

### Alice borrows "The Pragmatic Programmer" (book 4, one copy) for herself
POST {{host}}/api/v1/loans
Authorization: Basic {{alice}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-Request-Id: demo-borrow-1

{
  "bookId": 4,
  "memberId": 1
}

### Bob tries the same book -> 409 BOOK_UNAVAILABLE
POST {{host}}/api/v1/loans
Authorization: Basic {{bob}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookId": 4,
  "memberId": 2
}

### Alice tries to borrow for Bob -> 403
POST {{host}}/api/v1/loans
Authorization: Basic {{alice}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookId": 1,
  "memberId": 2
}

### Librarian borrows on behalf of Bob
POST {{host}}/api/v1/loans
Authorization: Basic {{librarian}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookId": 1,
  "memberId": 2
}

### Alice's loans (newest first)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/members/1/loans
Authorization: Basic {{alice}}

### Return loan 1 (Alice owns it)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/loans/1/return
Authorization: Basic {{alice}}

### Return it again -> 409 LOAN_ALREADY_RETURNED
POST {{host}}/api/v1/loans/1/return
Authorization: Basic {{alice}}

### Search loans by status: ACTIVE | OVERDUE | RETURNED (LIBRARIAN / ADMIN)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/loans?status=ACTIVE&sort=dueDate,asc
Authorization: Basic {{librarian}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- Observability (ADMIN)

### Business metrics: library_loans_*
GET {{host}}/actuator/prometheus
Authorization: Basic {{admin}}

### Build and git info
GET {{host}}/actuator/info
Authorization: Basic {{admin}}

### Health details (DB) are shown to ADMIN
GET {{host}}/actuator/health
Authorization: Basic {{admin}}
